WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:03.600
Let's embrace...

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.980
Being together like this...

00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:09.900
...is something I'll never forget!

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.310
Forever...

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:15.830
...under this sky...

00:00:15.830 --> 00:00:18.440
...we'll walk together!

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.130
In this beauty...

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.240
...that I'm dreaming...

00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.290
...the world's just a...

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:24.420
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.010
With more dreaming...

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:27.080
...and more loving...

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.170
...my heart is a...

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:29.390
...merry, merry-go-round!

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.690
Luvly, merry-go-round!

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.080
Getting ready for a good morning...

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:35.760
...I say 'good morning', then I chat and run.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.940
A lovely life every day...

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.640
...is my wish for you, my sweet heart!

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.740
A, B, C, D, E, F, G!

00:00:42.750 --> 00:00:45.390
A lack of vitamins isn't healthy.

00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:47.520
1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7!

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:50.600
Bring along your favorite and let's go!

00:00:53.080 --> 00:00:56.460
Rolling rainbow star!

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.830
If you go there...

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.830
...you'll surely find it!

00:01:02.840 --> 00:01:06.210
Lovely roller coaster!

00:01:06.210 --> 00:01:08.690
Under this sky...

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.340
...its a total pleasure!

00:01:13.610 --> 00:01:16.060
Being together like this...

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.590
...is something I'll never forget!

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.780
Under this sky...

00:01:25.780 --> 00:01:28.270
...we'll walk together!

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:36.480
At Kazuma-kun's elementary school, the teacher
he had a crush on, Tachikawa-sensei,

00:01:36.500 --> 00:01:38.730
was hit by a dart poisoned with curare.

00:01:39.790 --> 00:01:45.150
Fortunately she survived, but the scene
of the crime was extremely bizarre

00:01:46.130 --> 00:01:52.990
because the room, where the criminal who
blew the dart must have been, was totally sealed off

00:01:53.010 --> 00:01:55.620
and yet there was no trace of him.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:02:00.670
And the weapon used in this case, according to legend,

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:05.000
was a blowgun that was used to blow
darts in a masked curse ceremony.

00:02:14.790 --> 00:02:18.680
Sir, are these things used in a cursing ceremony?

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:20.560
Yes.

00:02:21.290 --> 00:02:24.270
The criminal tried to destroy the evidence, huh?

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:28.940
Destroy the evidence... You believe in the curse too?

00:02:29.840 --> 00:02:31.950
No I don't, but...

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:37.490
But first it was speaking with the dead and
now it's an cursed Amazonian blowgun,

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.620
you DDS guys always seem to get weird ones like this.

00:02:51.910 --> 00:02:59.430
Assistant Principal. I hear that, every day, you
go to Tachikawa-sensei's room on your rounds,

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:01.890
but what time is that, usually?

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:04.400
D-Don't get me wrong!

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:08.440
I'm not going out of some kind of ulterior
motive. I really am making my rounds!

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:11.740
Umm.

00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:14.950
Right then!

00:03:14.970 --> 00:03:18.120
Right about the time that she was involved
in that unfortunate accident.

00:03:20.350 --> 00:03:25.210
By the way, all those strange South American
and African tools in your storage room,

00:03:26.230 --> 00:03:28.250
I hear that's your hobby.

00:03:28.650 --> 00:03:32.090
Not a hobby so much as... for anthropological research!

00:03:32.570 --> 00:03:34.430
Do you believe in curses then?

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:38.140
No, it's just something I research!

00:03:41.580 --> 00:03:48.320
Iwadome-sensei, I hear that the poison on the
weapon, curare, was stolen from your room.

00:03:49.050 --> 00:03:49.940
Yes.

00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:53.650
But I have my license to possess
poisons and dangerous materials!

00:03:55.890 --> 00:03:59.030
By the way, and this is just a rumor,

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:02.450
but I heard that you pressured Tachikawa-sensei
to go out with you?

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:04.830
I did invite her to dinner,

00:04:05.360 --> 00:04:07.580
but that's not a crime!

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:11.260
Well no, but

00:04:11.990 --> 00:04:15.010
it looked like she really hated you.

00:04:16.950 --> 00:04:19.560
Excuse me for asking, but you and Ebe-sensei were...

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:22.940
Well she came onto me.

00:04:24.830 --> 00:04:28.360
Yes, I did date Iwadome-sensei.

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:33.320
Then did you have any trouble with
Tachikawa-sensei over that?

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:36.990
No, we're not  dating anymore.

00:04:41.310 --> 00:04:42.240
Um, sensei.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:46.620
That pendant you're wearing is the "Love Cupid Pendant”
that you see in the magazines all the time.

00:04:47.310 --> 00:04:48.210
It's supposed to bring you love from somebody.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.040
I didn't know.

00:04:51.780 --> 00:04:53.710
A friend gave it to me.

00:04:57.700 --> 00:05:00.970
Both the assistant principal and Iwadome-sensei 
were in love with Tachikawa-sensei,

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:02.560
but she didn't like either of them.

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:07.310
And at the same time, Ebe-sensei was jealous of her.

00:05:08.460 --> 00:05:14.190
Also the principal believes in curses, it looks like,
and Ebe-sensei's the type who believes in curses.

00:05:15.050 --> 00:05:20.620
Iwadome-sensei's a science teacher and unlikely
to, but he's used to handling poison.

00:05:30.650 --> 00:05:34.710
Hey, Ryuu-kun, it seemed like you were very
interested in the ventilators, but why?

00:05:36.030 --> 00:05:37.170
It's too perfect.

00:05:39.160 --> 00:05:43.680
This room, the kitchen, and the Home Ec. room:

00:05:44.540 --> 00:05:49.650
the doors and the windows are all way too airtight.

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:53.690
It's natural if we assume that it's like Kazuma said,

00:05:53.710 --> 00:05:58.700
to keep the cooking smells from
bothering the other classes.

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:04.490
In other words, there's not enough room for an
ant to get into this room, let alone a person.

00:06:05.060 --> 00:06:07.250
No room for an ant...

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:09.840
Whats wrong?

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:15.170
Carter Dickson wrote a book called
"He Wouldn't Kill Patience".

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:18.840
He wrote the basic plot together with Clayton Lawson.

00:06:19.450 --> 00:06:22.140
It had a sealed room that was actually
glued shut from the inside;

00:06:22.160 --> 00:06:24.010
a Sealed room trick that was just too perfect.

00:06:25.080 --> 00:06:26.560
Stop Looking like you know what he's talking about again.

00:06:28.460 --> 00:06:30.890
But to think that could actually exist.

00:06:31.740 --> 00:06:32.620
That's right.

00:06:33.210 --> 00:06:36.860
Realistically, you'd choose a more normal place.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:40.070
Could it possibly be a challenge to us Q-class?

00:06:42.010 --> 00:06:44.280
That was why the wiretap was there.

00:06:44.890 --> 00:06:46.120
That's over thinking things.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:47.420
But,

00:06:48.210 --> 00:06:48.840
I get it.

00:06:49.190 --> 00:06:49.710
Ryuu!

00:06:51.190 --> 00:06:54.380
The criminal knew it was a too-perfect sealed room.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:56.170
What's your proof?

00:06:56.610 --> 00:06:57.420
The ventilators?

00:06:57.860 --> 00:07:01.430
This is the cursed blowgun that they used.

00:07:02.820 --> 00:07:04.850
This... so it was cursed?

00:07:04.870 --> 00:07:05.680
Look in it.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:07.430
It's only enough room for air to pass.

00:07:08.500 --> 00:07:12.310
Is there anything that becomes possible
because the room's completely sealed?

00:07:14.340 --> 00:07:16.980
Something possible in an overly sealed room.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:23.360
The ones in the room then were Tachikawa-sensei,
Atsushi and Nozomi;

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:27.740
and they were making cookies in the microwave.

00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:31.210
All the ventilators in all three rooms were running.

00:07:33.770 --> 00:07:37.210
Now that I think about it, when I went
to get that cell phone I forgot...

00:07:38.820 --> 00:07:43.130
When I opened the door I felt a
draft coming in from the hallway.

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:45.890
What's wrong Kazuma?

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:47.190
No Way.

00:07:54.290 --> 00:07:55.100
I get it.

00:07:56.210 --> 00:07:59.650
The criminal's identity is clear.

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:00.540
WHAT!

00:08:01.260 --> 00:08:04.700
And so is the trick that made the impossible possible.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:09.790
I've solved its formula.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:12.200
But.

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:23.340
Kazuma, where are you going?

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:25.220
What?

00:08:25.780 --> 00:08:27.010
Leave it to Kazuma.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:28.220
But.

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:36.850
Takekawa General Hospital

00:08:38.500 --> 00:08:44.070
Takekawa Hitomi

00:08:41.550 --> 00:08:42.730
Come in, please.

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:47.660
Kazuma-kun.

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:53.580
Come in, sit over here.

00:08:54.190 --> 00:08:55.870
Yes, excuse me.

00:09:04.900 --> 00:09:05.880
What's wrong?

00:09:06.740 --> 00:09:08.640
You came here to talk to me, right?

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:12.030
Shall I make us some tea?

00:09:12.870 --> 00:09:16.640
I'm still a bit shaky but I can, at least, make tea.

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:25.690
Sensei.

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:28.200
You buy lottery tickets?

00:09:28.930 --> 00:09:30.450
Yeah, once in a while.

00:09:31.390 --> 00:09:33.700
Did you want money that bad?

00:09:35.550 --> 00:09:36.630
That's a bit of an exaggeration.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:38.770
Just over some lottery tickets.

00:09:38.770 --> 00:09:41.210
I'm not talking about them!

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:48.220
The person who shot that poison dart at you,

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:52.810
it was you yourself, Tachikawa-sensei!

00:09:54.750 --> 00:09:57.600
What are you talking about, Kazuma-kun?

00:09:57.620 --> 00:09:59.190
I'm the victim

00:09:59.210 --> 00:10:01.190
Tell the truth!

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.610
You take out an expensive insurance policy on yourself,

00:10:05.630 --> 00:10:08.780
fake being almost killed, and then
get the insurance money!

00:10:09.720 --> 00:10:12.950
That's a crime, insurance fraud!

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:23.130
My, my Kazuma-kun. You're going to DDS, right?

00:10:24.070 --> 00:10:27.550
That's why you're sounding like a detective, huh?

00:10:29.160 --> 00:10:31.640
You were right there with me, weren't you?

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:39.390
Atsushi-kun and Nozomi-san were there too,
and a poison dart struck me from behind.

00:10:43.040 --> 00:10:50.150
A policeman came by earlier and told me that somebody
had blown the dart from the next room.

00:10:52.350 --> 00:10:55.530
Do you really think I could've done it myself?

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:59.080
You're really smart, sensei.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:04.540
I was infuriated with the criminal
and investigated frantically.

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:07.630
And then I noticed something odd.

00:11:08.490 --> 00:11:09.380
Something odd?

00:11:09.860 --> 00:11:16.140
Yes. If the criminal was in the next room,

00:11:16.910 --> 00:11:18.890
he would've had to have vanished into thin air!

00:11:28.240 --> 00:11:29.510
Look at this.

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:33.430
These were on the floor next to the
door that the blowgun was stuck in.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:35.390
What is that?

00:11:36.250 --> 00:11:38.060
Little lumps of flour.

00:11:38.880 --> 00:11:42.980
They were used to seal the slight holes
created when the blowgun was wedged

00:11:43.010 --> 00:11:45.570
into the rubber packing of the sealed door.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.990
You wouldn't need these to just blow a blowgun.

00:11:51.720 --> 00:11:54.000
So why did the criminal need them?

00:11:54.720 --> 00:12:00.090
Because they were needed to keep something even
smaller than an ant from getting into the room.

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:02.420
What is that small thing?

00:12:04.930 --> 00:12:05.560
Air.

00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:11.510
All those rooms are extremely airtight.

00:12:12.660 --> 00:12:15.980
When it happened, the powerful ventilators were blowing

00:12:16.000 --> 00:12:18.560
and the air pressure of the three
rooms had decreased considerably.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:22.400
If the door to the Home Ec. room was opened, then

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:25.030
the air would instantly flow into the kitchen

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:28.570
and there would be a huge pressure difference
between the ends of the blowgun

00:12:28.590 --> 00:12:30.450
wedged into the door between the kitchen and prep room.

00:12:31.340 --> 00:12:36.080
You set the blowgun in the door there.

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:41.000
and turned on the Home Ec. and kitchen ventilators.

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:46.920
Of course, you set the blowgun to make sure the
arrow in it wouldn't come out the wrong way,

00:12:49.530 --> 00:12:56.840
and then you invited Nozomi and Atsushi in as witnesses.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:03.980
You waited for a good time, and then turned
on the ventilator to make the cookies

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:06.030
and the air pressure in the room started to go down.

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:12.160
Then you sat in your chair where
you knew the arrow would come

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:17.450
and waited for the assistant principal to come and
open the door at the same time he always did.

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:22.160
But something you didn't count on happening occurred.

00:13:23.190 --> 00:13:26.800
The assistant principal couldn't come that day

00:13:26.820 --> 00:13:30.800
because he was trying to chase us,
DDS, away from our investigation.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:37.930
Instead, I came to get my cell phone
and opened the door first.

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:49.030
In other words, I was the one who
was the "switch" to blow that dart!

00:13:51.640 --> 00:13:52.110
What?

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:54.660
When Kazuma opened the door?

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:58.130
Then the criminal "disappeared"?

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:02.870
It should've been the assistant principal who did that.

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:07.630
But when he opened the door, we all ran there

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:09.710
and we sealed off the door to the Home Ec. room,

00:14:10.780 --> 00:14:15.800
Because of that, the three rooms suddenly
turned into a “sealed room".

00:14:15.830 --> 00:14:19.180
and the "criminal" vanished.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.150
Kazuma knew that.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:26.940
Must be tough to have the teacher you love be a criminal.

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:34.660
If it weren't for that, even I would've thought
that the criminal was somebody I didn't know

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:38.990
and that they'd just gotten away.

00:14:46.480 --> 00:14:47.160
That's right.

00:14:48.940 --> 00:14:50.210
It's all like you said.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:55.840
But the most surprising thing was that
I had a genius like you as a student.

00:14:56.400 --> 00:14:57.340
Sensei.

00:14:58.450 --> 00:15:01.270
I wanted money no matter what.

00:15:03.540 --> 00:15:07.110
No matter how much I prayed
at the temple, I never got any.

00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:11.940
I had life insurance too, so I considered suicide.

00:15:12.840 --> 00:15:14.400
But that wouldn't do it.

00:15:17.720 --> 00:15:22.900
Then I heard the assistant principal talking
about curare in the teacher's room.

00:15:23.810 --> 00:15:28.840
The natives say that in a cursing
ritual the blowgun moves by itself

00:15:28.860 --> 00:15:33.130
and shoots darts on its own,

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.220
Don't scare me!

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:37.550
Jeez,

00:15:38.200 --> 00:15:42.640
I'd noticed the sealed
Home Ec. Rooms before, too.

00:15:45.250 --> 00:15:49.610
I thought up that trick.

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:56.240
If I was in an "accident", and was permanently
injured, I could get insurance money.

00:15:57.220 --> 00:15:57.950
And...

00:15:59.100 --> 00:16:06.330
So I stole the cursed blowgun from the storeroom
and the curare from the evidence room.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:11.000
I didn't know how strong the poison was.

00:16:12.280 --> 00:16:15.630
But you brought your friends from DDS

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:20.260
so I panicked.

00:16:21.280 --> 00:16:26.270
I had confidence in my trick, so I decided to chance it.

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:33.820
The worst part about it was having to
use my own Students in the trick.

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:38.570
That's fine.

00:16:39.470 --> 00:16:41.400
It's fine, but why?

00:16:42.520 --> 00:16:46.660
Why go through all that trouble
just to commit insurance fraud?

00:16:47.190 --> 00:16:50.000
I told you, I wanted money.

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:53.710
30,000,000 yen, as soon as possible.

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:56.010
But why?

00:16:58.360 --> 00:17:00.880
It's the cost of my kid's surgery.

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:08.730
I had somebody I was going to marry.

00:17:09.420 --> 00:17:11.480
I had his child.

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:16.400
I couldn't tell the school that I had got
pregnant before marriage, so I didn't.

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:19.740
My stomach never got that big.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:23.620
But he  died in an accident.

00:17:24.310 --> 00:17:26.750
The shock sent me into labor early.

00:17:27.810 --> 00:17:29.900
Your child...

00:17:31.360 --> 00:17:33.420
That was why I was on vacation.

00:17:33.440 --> 00:17:38.090
Then all the more. If you have a kid, then if you died...

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:41.430
Sensei, hang on!

00:17:42.120 --> 00:17:44.140
Please take me to Takekawa...

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:47.310
Is your child?

00:17:49.330 --> 00:17:54.640
So I had them take me here, to where my baby is.

00:18:00.370 --> 00:18:02.740
My baby was premature, and it
had a problem with its heart.

00:18:05.000 --> 00:18:07.490
If it doesn't get surgery soon

00:18:13.640 --> 00:18:15.540
I just wanted to save his baby.

00:18:20.360 --> 00:18:21.840
But it's all over.

00:18:22.780 --> 00:18:26.300
Without the insurance money I can't pay for the surgery.

00:18:28.660 --> 00:18:29.520
Or...

00:18:31.780 --> 00:18:34.400
Kazuma-kun, will you let me go?

00:18:44.430 --> 00:18:45.520
I'm sorry.

00:18:47.810 --> 00:18:51.040
Will you call the police?

00:18:59.740 --> 00:19:02.300
This is Tachikawa-san's baby.

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:22.640
So if Kazuma lets her go...

00:19:25.300 --> 00:19:27.320
Can a DDS student do that?

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:29.780
We left things to Kazuma.

00:19:30.680 --> 00:19:33.000
So, let's let him decide.

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:42.880
No matter what he decides, it'll be the right thing.

00:19:43.860 --> 00:19:44.340
Am I wrong?

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:47.430
That's right.

00:19:54.330 --> 00:19:56.440
Arara, you're in a good mood,

00:19:56.460 --> 00:19:58.560
Mijimi-chan! You're a good girl!

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:02.400
Shall I get you some milk?

00:20:13.060 --> 00:20:13.900
Hello?

00:20:21.900 --> 00:20:26.300
Then just as contacted, I will take Tachikawa-sensei
down to the station.

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:28.120
Thank you.

00:20:30.370 --> 00:20:32.000
This is the best way.

00:20:32.200 --> 00:20:32.850
Yeah.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:37.880
But to think Iwadome was a real stalker

00:20:41.160 --> 00:20:45.440
I found this receiver for a wiretap in your room!

00:20:45.470 --> 00:20:46.700
Confess!

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.280
I'm sorry!

00:20:49.930 --> 00:20:55.950
But she refused to respond to me.

00:20:56.880 --> 00:21:04.050
Ebe-sensei hated her for stealing her love
so much that she did a "Cursing Ritual”.

00:21:04.690 --> 00:21:07.660
I'm
sorry!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:11.640
But she didn't really mean to kill her.

00:21:12.490 --> 00:21:15.520
After the incident, she got scared

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:18.760
and tried to burn the implements in the incinerator.

00:21:30.550 --> 00:21:31.400
I'm sorry

00:21:34.850 --> 00:21:36.490
Thank you for turning yourself in.

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:40.750
I'm sorry to trouble you.

00:21:41.860 --> 00:21:42.830
Let's go.

00:21:43.360 --> 00:21:43.880
Yes.

00:21:50.070 --> 00:21:52.180
It's not insurance fraud,,

00:21:52.200 --> 00:21:55.300
so they said you'd probably just have to send some
documents to the prosecutor and that'll be it.

00:21:56.120 --> 00:22:00.140
We'll take care of your baby, then.

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:02.800
Thank you.

00:22:04.300 --> 00:22:07.060
Come on, don't cry so much.

00:22:07.090 --> 00:22:08.820
You still haven't fully healed yet.

00:22:09.540 --> 00:22:10.320
I'm sorry.

00:22:10.680 --> 00:22:12.320
Hey, that's a lottery ticket.

00:22:13.500 --> 00:22:14.870
They announced this yesterday.

00:22:15.420 --> 00:22:16.280
Did you win?

00:22:17.120 --> 00:22:18.420
I haven't seen it yet.

00:22:19.300 --> 00:22:20.280
I'm sure I didn't.

00:22:21.060 --> 00:22:23.080
I buy them every time they do them.

00:22:23.560 --> 00:22:28.380
I even have the winning numbers in my badge like this.

00:22:29.280 --> 00:22:30.090
Hmm...

00:22:36.820 --> 00:22:38.800
You won!

00:22:38.820 --> 00:22:39.970
30,000,000 yen!

00:22:41.040 --> 00:22:41.730
It's true.

00:22:41.750 --> 00:22:42.640
Amazing!

00:22:43.420 --> 00:22:44.350
30,000,000 yen?!

00:22:44.420 --> 00:22:45.560
Here!

00:22:49.380 --> 00:22:51.900
Oh God.Thank you!

00:22:52.720 --> 00:22:53.610
Thank you!

00:22:54.220 --> 00:22:56.240
Tachikawa-san!

00:23:04.180 --> 00:23:05.320
Young master.

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:13.000
Just as you requested, we purchased the 30,000,000
yen winning ticket, and gave it to Odajima-sama;

00:23:13.660 --> 00:23:15.590
but why would you make such a strange request?

00:23:16.520 --> 00:23:17.850
It's fine.

00:23:19.500 --> 00:23:22.600
Another good game and that'll make up for that.

00:23:23.250 --> 00:23:28.680
That's true. Your games are always such huge successes.

00:23:30.340 --> 00:23:31.230
You too.

00:23:45.590 --> 00:23:47.420
THOSE THINGS REFLECTED IN YOUR EYES...

00:23:47.420 --> 00:23:49.760
...ARE DESTINED TO FALL APART.

00:23:49.760 --> 00:23:52.430
NO! NO! NO! NO! BELIEVING IN THAT...

00:23:52.430 --> 00:23:54.090
...IS UP TO YOU.

00:23:54.090 --> 00:23:56.100
LOVE AND KINDNESS...

00:23:56.100 --> 00:23:58.390
...OFTEN STEM FROM SELFISHNESS.

00:23:58.390 --> 00:24:00.930
IF YOU STILL PURSUE THEM...

00:24:00.930 --> 00:24:02.730
...YOU'RE JUST WANDERING AIMLESSLY.

00:24:03.440 --> 00:24:06.980
IT CAN SEEM BOTH FAR AND NEAR...

00:24:06.980 --> 00:24:10.610
THAT PLACE WHERE LOVE LIVES.

00:24:11.650 --> 00:24:13.700
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:13.700 --> 00:24:16.120
...IS A MESSAGE TO YOU.

00:24:16.120 --> 00:24:18.240
YOU'RE USED TO WAITING FOR IT...

00:24:18.240 --> 00:24:19.790
...WITHOUT GIVING UP!

00:24:20.250 --> 00:24:22.460
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:22.460 --> 00:24:24.670
EVEN WHEN WE'RE LOST...

00:24:25.170 --> 00:24:26.880
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:26.880 --> 00:24:30.380
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO IT?

00:24:31.170 --> 00:24:33.340
THE UNSEEN STORY...

00:24:33.340 --> 00:24:35.260
EVEN WHEN WERE LOST...

00:24:35.260 --> 00:24:37.640
...CAN'T WE BELIEVE...

00:24:37.680 --> 00:24:40.470
...THAT WE CAN STILL DO?

00:24:47.680 --> 00:24:49.700
A mad prayer filled with a lust for radiance.

00:24:49.050 --> 00:24:56.580
Next Time

00:24:50.430 --> 00:24:52.910
This is the holy ground where the gods of jewelry dwell.

00:24:53.560 --> 00:24:55.910
And a bomber who's going to destroy the city!

00:24:56.690 --> 00:24:58.290
What's the next target?

00:24:58.900 --> 00:25:01.340
The steady countdown towards the explosion.

00:25:02.940 --> 00:25:03.920
Can we save the city?

00:25:04.650 --> 00:25:05.550
There's one answer!

00:25:07.280 --> 00:25:08.760
Work again today!

00:25:09.280 --> 00:25:12.140
At times like this I'm envious of all your wealth, Kazuma.

00:25:12.160 --> 00:25:13.430
That's not true.

00:25:14.540 --> 00:25:17.520
There's more things in this world
that you can't buy than you can.
